# Disable USB autosuspend globally, via udev.
#
# swarmarchy also drops `options usbcore autosuspend=-1` into /etc/modprobe.d, but
# that is IGNORED when usbcore is built into the kernel (the usual case on aarch64 /
# ALARM) -- module options only take effect for a loadable usbcore or via the kernel
# cmdline. This rule sets power/control=on on every USB device as it appears, which
# works regardless of built-in-vs-module. It prevents peripherals -- especially
# hubs/KVMs -- from autosuspending and dropping off the bus on idle. On the Yoga
# Slim 7x (X1E80100) an autosuspended USB-C KVM hub drops the DP-alt link with it and
# wedges the Adreno GMU (silent hard hang).
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", TEST=="power/control", ATTR{power/control}="on"
